<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iscor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as South African Iron and Steel Industrial Corporation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iscor, the South African Iron and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a> Industrial Corporation, was a state-owned steel company founded in 1928 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/j-b-m-hertzog">J. B. M. Hertzog</a>'s government to build a national steel industry. Its works at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> began production in 1934 and were followed by plants at Vanderbijlpark and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newcastle-upon-tyne">Newcastle</a>, and it provided protected employment for poor white workers. Privatised in 1989, it is now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcelormittal">ArcelorMittal</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</p></div>
